# Host crontab entry to drive `POST /poll` at 60-second cadence.
#
# Install on the Docker host with:
#     crontab -e     # then paste the line below and save
#
# Recommended baseline is every 60s. Host cron's minimum resolution IS
# one minute — sub-minute cadence needs two entries offset by
# `sleep 30 && ...` and rarely pays off.
#
# Flags on the curl command:
#   -f       fail on 4xx/5xx (so cron logs the failure)
#   -s -S    silent except errors (keeps the log tail readable)
#   -m 55    hard-timeout at 55s so a stuck tick doesn't overlap the
#            next cron trigger; 409 from single-flight is preferable
#            to two concurrent hangers
#   -w '%{http_code}\n'
#            append the HTTP status so `grep 409 zashiki-cron.log`
#            surfaces overlap events without needing to parse output
#
# The API-key value MUST match `HTTP_API_KEY` in the container's env.
# When bind_host is loopback inside the container's own namespace,
# reach it via the published host port (default 8080).

* * * * * curl -fsS -m 55 -w '%{http_code}\n' -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/poll -H "X-API-Key: change-me-to-a-strong-secret" >> /var/log/zashiki-cron.log 2>&1
